    "result_text": "There's a single test class, and it passes along with the full build.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe change adds a `selfLink` field of `/api/owners/{id}` to the owner GET response, satisfying the spec and the new `coreReturnsSelfLink` acceptance test (which creates an owner, then reads it back via `GET /api/owners/{id}` and asserts `$.selfLink`).\n\nTwo files touched, keeping structural impact low:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `selfLink` read-only string property to the `Owner` schema. This regenerates `OwnerDto` with `setSelfLink`, following the exact pattern of the other derived fields (`bulkSignupWarning`, `checkDigit`, `ageBand`, etc.) that also have no source on the entity.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../owner/RespondWithOwner.java`** \u2014 added one line, `dto.setSelfLink(\"/api/owners/\" + owner.getId());`, alongside the other derived-field setters. This function's only sibling is the small private `luhn` helper, so the surrounding complexity (WMC_other) paid for is minimal \u2014 no existing method was grown and no large class was touched.\n\nThe full test suite builds green (`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`).",
